  "body": "## Problem\n\n`fold_warnings_located` in `crates/ui/src/operations.rs` groups the warnings by a key. Two kinds on `main` use the same key:\n\n- `Warning::AvoidHit { part: FixturePart::Shank, .. }` gives `216 + 0 = 216` (the avoid range is `216..=220`).\n- `Warning::DrillUndersize { .. }` gives `216`.\n\nA group prints only the line of its first warning. When a program has the two warnings, the pane shows one line. The second finding is not visible. The `AvoidHit` finding is a blocking verdict for a protected \"Do not touch\" item.\n\n## Fix\n\nGive `DrillUndersize` a free key (for example `223`). Add a pin in `warning_fold_tests` that folds one `DrillUndersize` and one `AvoidHit` shank hit and asserts two lines.\n\n## Context\n\nThe clear-out refresh of PR #2836 found the defect. That refresh moved `UndercutLift` from `217` to `222` for the same reason. This issue is for the `DrillUndersize` key on `main` only.\n",
